Package: waydesk-server
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: José Mendonça <jmendonca@gmail.com>
Section: x11
Priority: optional
Depends: acl, waydesk-sway | sway, foot, libopenh264-8 (>= 2.6), libva2, libva-drm2, libgbm1, libdrm2, libpam0g, libpam-runtime, libxkbcommon0, openssl, systemd, adduser, systemd-zram-generator, pipewire, pipewire-pulse, pulseaudio-utils, wireplumber, wl-clipboard
Recommends: wireguard-tools, qrencode, intel-media-va-driver-non-free | intel-media-va-driver | mesa-va-drivers
Description: RDP server giving each account its own sway desktop
 Accounts log in over RDP with their normal password and get a private,
 headless sway session that survives disconnects. A small root helper checks
 passwords (PAM) and starts the sessions; the network-facing daemon runs as
 an unprivileged account.
 .
 Early software. Plain TLS login: `waydesk-admin access`, `cert` and `vpn` set who can
 reach it (this machine, a local network, a WireGuard VPN), what certificate clients check, and who may connect.
